{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "reconstructed_statement": "Let E be any real normed vector space whose additive group is a normed additive commutative group, with a complete norm topology, a second-countable topology, and a measurable structure equal to its Borel structure. Let mu be any Gaussian probability measure on E, in the sense that every continuous real linear functional has a Gaussian pushforward; its mean is unrestricted and degeneracy is allowed. Let L be any nonnegative real Lipschitz constant, including L = 0, and let f: E -> R satisfy the global bound |f(x) - f(y)| <= L ||x - y|| for all x,y in E. Then f is Bochner integrable with respect to mu, and for every real t, including negative t and t = 0, the function x |-> exp(t (f(x) - m)), where m = integral_E f(z) dmu(z) is the actual mean of f under mu, is Bochner integrable with respect to mu. The conclusion is integrability of each such centered exponential; it supplies no quantitative bound on its integral.",
  "semantic_slots": {
    "objects": "A real normed vector space E; a Gaussian probability measure mu on E; a nonnegative real constant L; a real-valued function f; the actual scalar mean m = integral f dmu; centered exponential functions indexed by real t.",
    "domains": "E: Type with NormedAddCommGroup, NormedSpace R, CompleteSpace, SecondCountableTopology, MeasurableSpace and BorelSpace. mu: Measure E with IsGaussian. L: nonnegative real numbers (NNReal). f: E -> R. t: all R.",
    "quantifiers": "Universally quantified E and all listed ambient structures, mu with its Gaussian instance, L and f satisfying LipschitzWith L f. The conclusion is a conjunction: Integrable f mu, and for every real t, Integrable (x |-> exp(t (f(x) - integral f dmu))) mu.",
    "assumptions": "Completeness, second countability and Borel measurability of E; genuine Gaussian probability law (possibly noncentered or degenerate); global L-Lipschitz f, with L >= 0 and L = 0 allowed. No centered-law, finite-dimensional, covariance normalization, or separately assumed mean or moment condition.",
    "conclusion": "The actual f is Bochner integrable and every centered exponential built from its own mean is Bochner integrable under the same mu. This is not an asserted sharp bound on the exponential integral.",
    "scopes_senses": "The conjunction establishes integrability of f and then quantifies all signed real t. Centering uses integral_E f(z) dmu(z) of this same function and law. Integrability is genuine Bochner integrability, not a placeholder or supplied certificate. Gaussianity concerns all continuous real linear functional pushforwards.",
    "constant_dependencies": "Only the arbitrary nonnegative Lipschitz parameter L occurs in the premise; it may be zero. The conclusion provides no explicit MGF constant, covariance parameter, rate or dimension law. E need not be finite-dimensional, and no normalization of its Gaussian law is asserted."
  },
